{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_l46xmwe2nzxfw3mqknwutvsmg6ocdard4h62t3xm5wshg6lc4agq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything works. The implementation:\n\n1. **Parser** — handles whitespace skipping (matching C's `<= 32` byte rule), null/true/false literals, numbers (with optional sign, fractional, and exponent), strings (with all standard escapes plus `\\uXXXX` unicode + UTF-16 surrogate pairs), arrays, and nested objects.\n2. **`parse(input, require_end)`** — drives the parser; if `require_end` is true, asserts that nothing but whitespace remains.\n3. **Pretty/compact printers** — `print_unformatted` produces single-line output (no spaces), `print_formatted` uses tabs for indent (matching the C output style with `:\\t` and `, ` between array items, `\\n` between object members, and special-cased empty arrays/objects).\n4. **Number formatting** — emits integer form when the value is exactly an integer in safe range, otherwise Rust's default `f64` `Display`, which is JSON-valid and round-trips.\n5. **String escaping** — handles `\"`, `\\`, `\\b\\f\\n\\r\\t`, and other sub-32 control characters via `\\u00XX`.\n6. **`CJson` API** — `create_*` constructors, `add_item_to_array`/`add_item_to_object`, `get_array_size`, `get_array_item`, `get_object_item` (case-insensitive lookup like cJSON).\n7. **Errors** — `CJsonError` `Display` implementation covers every variant; the `std::error::Error` impl is preserved.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()` placeholders. The pre-existing test (`test_example`) passes, and `test_main` runs cleanly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":56860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1083,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nu